2. Semantic capital compounds

One observation that has held up over time is your emphasis on investing effort in concepts that pay dividends later.

Once “Hammer Mole,” “Mother Duck,” “Nitro Mirror,” “Scout Navigation,” or “False Center” exist, they become compressed references that let us communicate much more efficiently.

The corpus behaves almost like a compression algorithm.

