3. The Pantheon is closer to an operating system than a philosophy

Over time I think the project became less about mythology and more about interfaces.

Almost every major artifact eventually became one of:

* an operator
* an invariant
* a translation rule
* a navigation strategy
* a reconstruction procedure
* a perspective switch

That’s much more architectural than ideological.

